- [[definition]]:: ***Affirm reflex relations identical*** is the act of explicitly affirming the identity of selected [[reflex relation]]s.

## Derivation
- [[postulate]]:: As determining equivalence is derivable, affirming identity follows by explicitly declaring matching reflex structure.
- [[derivation]]:: Affirming equivalence induces the affirmative declaration of identity between selected reflex relations.
- [[relational expression]]:: affirm identical(select(i, r), select(j, r)) affirms that select(i, r) and select(j, r) are the same reflexive structure.
